turns that into a refusal naming the file. The README floor and the approval view's need prose read through them with the file they resolved, and baseline_snapshot._needs_at, the record's history reader, names the commit and the file. load_need_tier(path, id_col) is the one need-tier row loader: it resolves the needs file under NEED_CARRIERS, returns the TOML file's tier through load, and under markdown returns the needs as rows keyed SN-ID under today's column names (status read off the section) and no stakeholders. baseline_snapshot._tier_rows reads every NEED_TIERS tier through it, on the live side and the recorded side alike, and _copy_file finds the needs registry or its copy under either carrier.\"\"\"","+code_symbol = \"needs_from_text/needs_or_refuse/load_need_tier/_markdown_need_rows/tier_carriers/tier_rows_from_text/_needs_at/_tier_rows/_copy_file\"","+detail = \"\"\"spine_carrier.needs_from_text(text, carrier) reads .toml text as its need tables only and .md text as the legacy tables, and raises on a .toml text that does not parse or on a carrier the need tier does not have; needs_or_refuse(path, text) takes the carrier from the path's suffix and turns that into a refusal naming the file. The README floor and the approval view's need prose read through them with the file they resolved, and baseline_snapshot._needs_at, the record's history reader, names the commit and the file. load_need_tier(path, id_col) is the one need-tier row loader: it resolves the needs file under NEED_CARRIERS, returns the TOML file's tier through load, and under markdown returns the needs as rows keyed SN-ID under today's column names (status read off the section) and no stakeholders. tier_carriers chooses the supported carriers for every tier (need carriers for SN-ID and STK-ID, row carriers otherwise), and tier_rows_from_text reads one tier's registry text under the carrier its file was read from: TOML, CSV, or the legacy markdown needs carrier. baseline_snapshot._tier_rows reads every NEED_TIERS tier through load_need_tier, on the live side and the recorded side alike, and _copy_file finds the needs registry or its copy under either carrier.\"\"\""," rationale = \"\"\"Choosing the carrier by sniffing the text read a TOML file declaring no need as markdown, so a table row in a string became a need, and read a malformed TOML file as markdown instead of refusing it; the reader holding the file knows its carrier, so no guess is needed. The row loader the other tiers share knows TOML and CSV alone, so a needs file still on the supported markdown carrier yielded no rows on either side of the comparison and a drifted need read as none.\"\"\""," status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-006\""]},{"oldStart":2850,"oldLines":9,"newStart":2850,"newLines":9,"lines":[" [design.LLR-278]"," sr_refs = [\"SR-178\", \"SR-228\"]"," title = \"An adjudication re-attestation constrained at merge\"","-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/acceptance_record.py\"","-code_symbol = \"first_approval_scope/adjudication_approval_refusal/merge_approval_refusal/_reattested_registries/amendment_scope/reattested_between/_wrote_ledger/verdict_rulings/_tier_of/_below_approval/_held_row_line/_held_act_lines/held_reattest_refusal/reattest_scope_refusal\"","-detail = \"acceptance_record.merge_approval_refusal calls reattest_scope_refusal and held_reattest_refusal for an adjudication lane, and they act only when the merge delta wrote the act ledger. reattested_between reads the ledger at the merge base and the head and takes the ids re-attested by the entries whose seq the base does not hold, refusing by name when either side does not parse. Every such id outside amendment_scope - the union of the claimed amendment rows' own amendment scope, including their amendment:<id> tokens when a combined sitting claims them, empty when none is claimed - is refused by name before the first-approval judgement runs. For each re-attested row whose tier the dial at trunk's tip holds - trunk's tip being the commit the merge lands on, not the merge base - held_reattest_refusal refuses the row by name when it is below approval or absent at the head, when its act names no verdict, or when verdict_rulings, reading the named verdict at the head, does not rule the row CLARITY; a row tagged both MEANING and CLARITY reads MEANING. An act that both approves rows and re-attests rows, claimed either by two single-kind rows or by one combined sitting's per-kind tokens, merges when each half lies inside its claiming row's own kind scope, whether their rows are in one registry or different ones; an id under another combined kind authorizes neither half, a snapshot is WIDENED only when the act neither flipped nor re-attested a row in that registry, and every held re-attestation has its CLARITY verdict.\"","+module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/acceptance_record.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/verdict.py\"","+code_symbol = \"first_approval_scope/adjudication_approval_refusal/merge_approval_refusal/_registry_identity/_reattested_registries/amendment_scope/reattested_between/_wrote_ledger/verdict_rulings/_tier_of/_below_approval/_held_row_line/_held_act_lines/held_reattest_refusal/reattest_scope_refusal\"","+detail = \"acceptance_record.merge_approval_refusal calls reattest_scope_refusal and held_reattest_refusal for an adjudication lane, and they act only when the merge delta wrote the act ledger. reattested_between reads the ledger at the merge base and the head and takes the ids re-attested by the entries whose seq the base does not hold, refusing by name when either side does not parse. Every such id outside amendment_scope - the union of the claimed amendment rows' own amendment scope, including their amendment:<id> tokens when a combined sitting claims them, empty when none is claimed - is refused by name before the first-approval judgement runs. For each re-attested row whose tier the dial at trunk's tip holds - trunk's tip being the commit the merge lands on, not the merge base - held_reattest_refusal refuses the row by name when it is below approval or absent at the head, when its act names no verdict, or when verdict_rulings, reading the named verdict at the head, does not rule the row CLARITY; a row tagged both MEANING and CLARITY reads MEANING. An act that both approves rows and re-attests rows, claimed either by two single-kind rows or by one combined sitting's per-kind tokens, merges when each half lies inside its claiming row's own kind scope, whether their rows are in one registry or different ones; an id under another combined kind authorizes neither half, a snapshot is WIDENED only when the act neither flipped nor re-attested a row in that registry identity: every carrier path of an authorized registry, including a deleted obsolete carrier copy, is authorized, while an unauthorized registry's copy is WIDENED on every carrier path, and every held re-attestation has its CLARITY verdict.\""," rationale = \"\"\"At merge the first-approval scope check read flips alone, and a re-attestation moves no cell, so an amendment act could re-anchor rows its verdict never ruled. The act ledger is the one record naming the rows each act re-attested, which makes the scope checkable where the merge is judged; a lane claiming no amendment has ruled no amended text, so it may re-anchor none.\"\"\""," status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-006\""]},{"oldStart":3244,"oldLines":8,"newStart":3244,"newLines":8,"lines":[" sr_refs = [\"SR-156\"]"," title = \"A Done-when blessing binds the exact changed checklist\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/done_when.py\"","-code_symbol = \"bound_items/digest/covering/blessing/blessing_owed/hold_reason/spec_at/lane_hold/staged_closes\"","-detail = \"bound_items reads each current Done-when item that only ticks or evidences a claim-time item as that claim-time item; digest binds the work-item id and those items as sha256 truncated to 16 hexadecimal characters. covering reads verdict lines under review records and decision entries: a DONE-WHEN line with outcome CLARITY, BLESSED or SUCCESSOR and the digest covers it, as does an owner-confirmed or owner-overruled decision entry carrying that digest; an unseen entry or retired reviewed key does not. blessing_owed reports only a readable current checklist that differs from a readable claim and has no cover; unreadable trees are unblessed and a missing claim or current checklist owes nothing. spec_at reads the active or closed specification at a revision, lane_hold compares a lane's claim at its base with its current or closed copy at the requested revision, and staged_closes identifies index moves from active into any terminal home: docs/archive/work/complete, partial or cancelled, or the legacy docs/work equivalent.\"","+code_symbol = \"bound_items/digest/covering/_copy_at/claim_copy/unreadable_reason/blessing/blessing_owed/hold_reason/spec_at/_wi_hold/lane_hold/staged_closes\"","+detail = \"bound_items reads each current Done-when item that only ticks or evidences a claim-time item as that claim-time item; digest binds the work-item id and those items as sha256:<16 hex>. covering reads verdict lines under review records and decision entries: a DONE-WHEN line with outcome CLARITY, BLESSED or SUCCESSOR and the digest covers it, as does an owner-confirmed or owner-overruled decision entry carrying that digest; an unseen entry or retired reviewed key does not. claim_copy returns absent when its readable revision has no claimed specification for the work item, which releases every hold and produces neither a mint nor a brief; it returns unreadable when the revision or listed copy cannot be read, and unreadable_reason makes that a named hold at dispatch, hand close and merge and a mint or brief refusal. _copy_at gives both claim and current reads found, absent, or unreadable forms. blessing_owed owes when a readable current specification differs from a readable claim and has no cover; deleting its Done-when section reports every claimed item changed. An absent claim releases only for a row never claimed through that lane; an unreadable claim, unreadable current copy, or claimed row with no current active or closed specification holds naming why. spec_at returns path, text and why, and lane_hold compares a lane's claim at its base with its current or closed copy at the requested revision, and staged_closes identifies index moves from active into any terminal home: docs/archive/work/complete, partial or cancelled, or the legacy docs/work equivalent.\""," rationale = \"The same changed checklist is consulted at dispatch, hand close, merge and adjudication. One digest and covering predicate keep readers from accepting different texts or treating a verdict about an earlier text as a release.\""," test_refs = \"TC-325, TC-326\""," status = \"Drafted\""]},{"oldStart":3254,"oldLines":11,"newStart":3254,"newLines":11,"lines":[" "," [design.LLR-308]"," sr_refs = [\"SR-156\"]","-title = \"Done-when and combined adjudication briefs preserve scope and grammar\"","-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/adjudicate_brief.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/sitting.py\"","-code_symbol = \"done_when_values/_subject_claim/_spec_context/requested_kinds/_named_kinds/_sitting_scopes/combined_values/_sitting_refusal;scopes/sections/own_section/brief_scope\"","-detail = \"The done-when class accepts exactly one work item in Adjudicates, reads its claim at the lane integration base while active or at the commit that added the active copy after closure, refuses an unreadable claim, missing Context, or unchanged checklist, and renders both item lists, their changes, the LLR-307 digest, and the spec Context clipped with any cut stated. Its verdict grammar requires DONE-WHEN, one of CLARITY, BLESSED or SUCCESSOR, and changes and digest counters. A combined class accepts only amendment:<id>, first-approval:<id> and done-when:<id> Adjudicates tokens; it composes each named class through compose with that section's verdict path in fixed amendment, first-approval, done-when order, and refuses whole if any section cannot compose. Its verdict is checked against the kinds requested by its composed brief: it refuses no requested kinds, a different SITTING: JUDGED kind list, or anything other than exactly one heading per requested kind; each section passes that class's grammar. Both classes are routed and retainable through BRIEF_PROMPTS.\"","-rationale = \"A Done-when verdict must show and bind the exact text the holds evaluate. Combining checkpoint judgements may share a sitting, but must not fork their scope or relax a constituent grammar.\"","+title = \"Done-when adjudication brief binds its claim and context\"","+module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/adjudicate_brief.py\"","+code_symbol = \"done_when_values/_subject_claim/_spec_context\"","+detail = \"The done-when class accepts exactly one work item in Adjudicates, reads its claim at the lane integration base while active or at the commit that added the active copy after closure, refuses an unreadable claim, missing Context, or unchanged checklist, and renders both item lists, their changes, the LLR-307 digest, and the spec Context clipped at CANDIDATE_CLIP (120 lines), with any cut stated. Its verdict grammar requires DONE-WHEN, one of CLARITY, BLESSED or SUCCESSOR, and changes and digest fields. The class is routed and retainable through BRIEF_PROMPTS.\"","+rationale = \"A Done-when verdict must show and bind the exact text the holds evaluate. The brief supplies the claim and bounded purpose context a judge needs to distinguish a clarification from a moved scope.\""," test_refs = \"TC-327\""," status = \"Drafted\""," component = \"CMP-008\""]},{"oldStart":3275,"oldLines":3,"newStart":3275,"newLines":15,"lines":[" status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6","+","+[design.LLR-310]","+sr_refs = [\"SR-232\"]","+title = \"Combined sitting composes and validates kind-scoped adjudications\"","+module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/adjudicate_brief.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/sitting.py\"","+code_symbol = \"requested_kinds/_named_kinds/_sitting_scopes/combined_values/_sitting_refusal;scopes/sections/own_section/brief_scope\"","+detail = \"A combined class accepts only amendment:<id>, first-approval:<id> and done-when:<id> Adjudicates tokens; it composes each named class through compose with that section's verdict path in fixed amendment, first-approval, done-when order, and refuses whole if any section cannot compose. Its verdict is checked against the kinds requested by its composed brief: it refuses no requested kinds, a different SITTING: JUDGED kind list, or anything other than exactly one heading per requested kind; each section passes that class's grammar. Token and section parsing are shared by composition, validation, act scopes and merge-time minting; the class is routed and retainable through BRIEF_PROMPTS.\"","+rationale = \"A shared checkpoint reduces adjudication launches only if no constituent judgement loses its scope or grammar. One parser prevents composition, validation and later acts from interpreting the same sitting differently.\"","+test_refs = \"TC-327\"","+status = \"Drafted\"","+component = \"CMP-008\"","+phase = 6"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-841\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-841\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-841\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml"]}}}
